; SPIKE godot-test1-5u3.1, and since bd godot-test1-5u3.2 a CI DEPENDENCY —
; do not delete this scene with the spike tooling. It is deliberately NOT in
; player_controller's CHARACTERS list, so the game is byte-for-byte unchanged by
; its presence, but two things reach it: scripts/style_shots.gd's `body=skinned`
; column, and `gait_selfcheck.gd` check 8, which is the ONLY thing in the suite
; that exercises the skinned pose driver and fails outright if this file is gone.
; When style_shots' spike column retires (bd 5u3.3), check 8 is the last reader.
;
; `Body` stays even though the mesh needs no wrapper: the landing squash writes
; Body.position.y and capture_rest_pose reads Body.rotation, so every hero scene
; in this game has one (epic 5u3's notes). The .glb instance carries NO basis —
; a SKINNED glTF is exported Y-up and placed by its own root node, so the
; Rx(-90) every UNRIGGED part scene applies here would lay the hero on his face.

